# The license field is left out on purpose. In CFF a list of licenses
# means "any one of these", and this repository uses two licenses at
# once: one for the hardware and one for everything else. See README.md
# and REUSE.toml.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these designs, firmware or documentation, please cite them as below."
title: "tangible-controls: hand-held controls for the CAD A11y viewer"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Felix
    family-names: Hähnlein
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3484-4004"
  - given-names: Carlos E.
    family-names: Tejada
repository-code: "https://github.com/cad-accessibility/tangible-controls"
abstract: >-
  Open hardware input devices for CAD A11y, an accessible 3D model viewer
  for blind and low-vision people. A 3D-printed cube with a WitMotion
  WT901BLECL Bluetooth motion sensor switches the viewer to the standard
  view of whichever face points up, and an Adafruit Slider Trinkey sets
  the slice depth. The repository holds the CAD exports, parts lists,
  firmware and text-first build instructions.
keywords:
  - accessibility
  - blind
  - low vision
  - tangible user interface
  - open hardware
  - 3D printing
  - CAD
  - CircuitPython
